refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public DirectoryIterator::__construct stringdirectory
Constructs a new directory iterator from a path.

&reftitle.parameters;




   directory


     The path of the directory to traverse.

&reftitle.errors;
Throws an UnexpectedValueException if the directory does not exist.
Throws a ValueError if the directory is an empty string.

&reftitle.changelog;







     &Version;
     &Description;





     8.0.0

      Now throws a ValueError if
      directory is an empty string;
      previously it threw a RuntimeException.

  &reftitle.examples;



    A DirectoryIterator::__construct example

      This example will list the contents of the directory containing the script.



<?php
$dir = new DirectoryIterator(dirname(__FILE__));
foreach ($dir as $fileinfo) {
    if (!$fileinfo->isDot()) {
        var_dump($fileinfo->getFilename());
    }
}
?>
